From dc32d8dbfcd16f8b2977ae53b9d612cf38385817 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:38:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/36] Tests for the studio level, no-backend state first

Fifteen suites in the critical harness. The panel ones mount the real React
tree and read the text off the page, because the claim is that a refused
parameter carries its reason IN THE TEXT and a tooltip satisfies a unit test
while failing a reader who never hovers.

Two things the tests caught: a batch issued as four calls landed as four
batches of one in the results grid, and an X/Y/Z plot did the same for every
cell, so both now share one stamp - a grid whose cells arrive separately is a
column of single pictures. The cell's axis values ride on the row as well, so
the grid is labelled.
